    "ts": "2026-07-28T14:01:22+00:00",
    "headline": "Hedge funds on track for another stellar year on AI boom",
    "summary": "Global hedge funds are on track for another blockbuster year, as they look to surpass their returns from 2025 after an artificial intelligence boom buoyed first-half ‌performance for money managers across most investment strategies, according to a Goldman Sachs note sent to ‌clients that was seen by Reuters.  During the first six months of this year, hedge funds returned an average of 7%, well above the 10-year ​average of 4.1%, according to the Goldman report.  \"The first half of 2026 was notably strong for risk assets – an equity market rally ‌helped to offset softer fixed income performance, ⁠propelling a 60/40 passive portfolio to a return of 5.7% – but in spite of this, hedge funds continued their run of outperformance,\" Goldman said.",
    "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/hedge-funds-track-another-stellar-140122370.html",
    "source": "Reuters",
    "provider": "yfinance",
    "raw": {
